From ebfd0fe71d1e1a9d50457ac83861369d5269a9a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:11:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Collect consecutive small writes of a handle into whole
 records (redox-rpi #16)

Every write call is its own transaction, which rewrites the whole record
it touches (up to 128 KiB) plus node, tree path, allocator log and header.
A file written in 4 KiB calls costs about 28 times its size on the disk.

The scheme now keeps the consecutive writes of one handle after the first
one in memory and writes them when a record is complete, before any other
request, and on close.
